-- 🚨 KNOWN-BAD LEDGER ROW (#1182 / #1265 class, OPEN): this is a DIFFERENT,
-- PRE-EXISTING coverage gap from the #1276/#1386 rows in this file -- NOT
-- something S-alias-supply drained, and NOT something its fix touches. That
-- fix repairs the CHECKED half (impl-obligation existence); this pins the
-- DISPATCH half (which impl's body actually RUNS) still disagreeing with it.
--
-- `Blob` implements BOTH `IA` and `IB`. `A.mth Blob` and `B.mth Blob` are
-- alias-qualified calls that name TWO DIFFERENT interfaces. Correct answer:
-- 1 then 2 (each call dispatches to the impl its own alias names). OBSERVED
-- (still, on this binary): 1 then 1 -- `B.mth Blob` silently runs `IA`'s
-- body on check, run, AND build alike, because `renameAliasedMethods`
-- erases the alias to a bare `mth` before dispatch is decided, and ordinary
-- dispatch has no per-alias-occurrence discriminator.
--
-- Witness from F-fix-alias-collision's report (Note N1), confirmed
-- reproducing identically at both the pre-sprint merge-base `9824e65b` and
-- the sprint head -- neither this sprint's fix nor the alias-collision fix
-- caused it. THIS ROW IS EXPECTED TO STAY GREEN (i.e. keep reproducing the
-- WRONG value) until #1182/#1265 land; a value change here is the signal to
-- re-pin it, not a regression in this gate.
import ifa.{IA}
import ifb.{IB}
import ifa as A
import ifb as B

public export data Blob = Blob

export impl IA Blob where
  mth b = 1

export impl IB Blob where
  mth b = 2

main =
  let _ = println (A.mth Blob)
  println (B.mth Blob)
